Title: LSU Impressive Record | the LSU Foundation
Chunks: 0
As a new academic year begins, we invite you to learn of Louisiana State University's latest impressive statistics and great accomplishments, which are made possible by legacies such as yours.
LSU...
*   is the flagship institution of the state of Louisiana;  
*   is 1 of only 25 universities nationwide holding both land-grant and sea-grant status;  
*   is the only public university in the state designated as a research-extensive institution;  
*   is bringing in more than $120 million annually in outside research grants and contracts, a significant factor for the Louisiana economy;  
*   injects more than $500 million into the Baton Rouge economy annually;  
*   boasts impressive accomplishments among faculty members, including 2 Pulitzer Prizes and 1 Fullbright Distinguished Chair;  
*   has produced a number of distinguished undergraduates, including 14 Astronaut Scholars, 16 Critical Language Scholars, 9 DAAD Scholars, 42 Goldwater Scholars, 2 Knight-Hennessy Scholars, 6 Marshall Scholars, 1 Schwarzman Scholar, 13 Truman Scholars, 21 Udall Scholars and 14 Rhodes Scholars;  
*   has the second fastest computer at any academic institution worldwide. The supercomputer named "SuperMike" is 1,000 times faster than a contemporary desktop computer;  
*   has won 40 national championships in its athletic history and is tied for the most national titles in the Southeastern Conference.

